ID: Ch8-Languages-success
TEXT:

 

The ancient syntax falls into place as I study the glyphs. The inscription reads: "If you enjoy unearthing secrets, strike each of these glyphs in rapid sequence."

"Well?" Daren asks, leaning over my shoulder. "What does it say?"

choice("Follow the instructions written on the wall", Ch8-Follow, v_current_scene = Ch8-Follow, v_ch8_first_puzzle = 1)
choice("Translate the phrase to Daren, but don't touch the glyphs", Ch8-Translate, v_current_scene = Ch8-Translate, v_ch8_first_puzzle = 1)
choice("Tell Daren it's some cryptic warning, and don't touch the glyphs", Ch8-Cryptic, v_current_scene = Ch8-Cryptic, v_ch8_first_puzzle = 2)


ID: Ch8-Follow
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch8_first,1)
achievement("First piece of the puzzle",v_ac_ch8_first)
 I tap the carved symbols one after another in a swift sequence.

A soft click echoes inside the wall. The carved stone recedes into the masonry, and two small objects pop out from the recess before the block slides flush again. I scoop them from the floor—a carved tile that interlocks like a puzzle piece, and a rolled strip of vellum.

The script on the vellum is common tongue: "Collect every piece of the puzzle, and I shall share my greatest secret. I have concealed one within each monument I designed."

It is signed simply: "The Architect."

"All right," Daren says, watching as I pocket both items. "First, what did the wall say, and second, what did you just pocket?"

"The wall promised a secret if pressed in sequence. The note claims whoever gathers all the puzzle pieces learns the architect's grand secret."

"Utterly useless," Daren mutters, shaking his head as he turns back down the hall. "Why I expect tactical advantages from dungeon graffiti is beyond me. We need to—"

Daren cuts off, freezing mid-stride. Blocking the corridor is a barefoot girl barely four feet tall, standing with her hands clasped behind her back and a bright grin on her face. She wears voluminous, colorful circus-style trousers, a simple gray tank top, and a polished golden amulet resting on her chest. Her bright red hair cascades nearly to her waist. She looks nine or ten at most, yet no protective ward triggers in my mind. She isn't registered as a local civilian.

"Hello!" she chirps, tilting her head.

"Where in the gods' names did you drop from?" Daren asks, his hand instinctively twitching toward his hilt.

"There!" She points a finger straight up at a ragged hole in the stone ceiling.

"Right," Daren says, blinking. "And what are you doing in an abandoned dungeon?"

"We were training in the chamber above when we heard voices down here. I'm Flower. Pleased to meet you!"

"Hold on," Daren says, holding up a palm. "Who is 'we'?"

Flower stiffens, her cheerful smile twitching.

"Did I say 'we'?" Her laugh is quick and nervous. "I meant 'I.' I was training upstairs. No 'we.' Just me. Just I."

