ID: Ch8-Translate
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch8_first,1)
achievement("First piece of the puzzle",v_ac_ch8_first)
 "It says: 'If you like discovering secrets, tap each of these glyphs in rapid succession.' "

"So why aren't you pressing them?" Daren asks.

"Could be a pressure-plate trap."

"Right! What better bait for a dungeon trap than an inscription in a dead tongue nobody reads?"

"Given that this was carved two thousand years ago, it wasn't a dead tongue when they built the place—"

"Move aside, I'll do it myself," Daren says, shoving past me to rap the symbols.

A soft click echoes inside the wall. The carved stone recedes into the masonry, and two small objects pop out from the recess before the block slides flush again. Daren scoops them up, scans the vellum, and thrusts both into my hands with an exasperated groan.

"Useless!"

The script on the vellum is common tongue: "Collect every piece of the puzzle, and I shall share my greatest secret. I have concealed one within each monument I designed."

