ID: Ch8-Cryptic
TEXT:

 "It just says: 'Turn back now, before it's too late. You have been warned.' "

"Naturally," Daren mutters, turning back down the hall. "Why I expect tactical advantages from dungeon graffiti is beyond me. We need to—"

Daren cuts off, freezing mid-stride. Blocking the corridor is a barefoot girl barely four feet tall, standing with her hands clasped behind her back and a bright grin on her face. She wears voluminous, colorful circus-style trousers, a simple gray tank top, and a polished golden amulet resting on her chest. Her bright red hair cascades nearly to her waist. She looks nine or ten at most, yet no protective ward triggers in my mind. She isn't registered as a local civilian.

"Hello!" she chirps, tilting her head.

"Where in the gods' names did you drop from?" Daren asks, his hand instinctively twitching toward his hilt.

"There!" She points a finger straight up at a ragged hole in the stone ceiling.

"Right," Daren says, blinking. "And what are you doing in an abandoned dungeon?"

"We were training in the chamber above when we heard voices down here. I'm Flower. Pleased to meet you!"

"Hold on," Daren says, holding up a palm. "Who is 'we'?"

Flower stiffens, her cheerful smile twitching.

"Did I say 'we'?" Her laugh is quick and nervous. "I meant 'I.' I was training upstairs. No 'we.' Just me. Just I."

choice("Continue", Ch8-Training, v_current_scene = Ch8-Training)


ID: Ch8-Training
TEXT:

 "What do you mean by training?" Kate asks her.

"Acrobatics, mostly!" Flower beams. "These ruins are packed with ancient traps. I practice dodging swinging blades with backflips and sprinting along the walls. It's fantastic!"

"Traps?" Kate's brow furrows.

"Lined wall to wall! You really have to watch your footing if you don't know the layout. Are you here exploring?"

"Not by choice," Kate says. "The forest beasts captured us and locked us in a holding cell. We're searching for the central control hub to disable the collars on our necks. Do you know where it is?"

"Control room?" Flower taps her chin in thought. "Oh! The chamber with all the levers and glowing switches! I know the way. Follow me!"

She spins on her bare heel and trots down the corridor. Daren leans close to my ear, his voice barely a murmur.

"Something is off. The tournament spell isn't reacting to her presence at all. No warning, no hostility ward. Why?"

choice(""Maybe she's an animal in disguise."", Ch8-Disguise, v_current_scene = Ch8-Disguise)
choice(""Maybe she's also participating in the tournament."", Ch8-Participating, v_current_scene = Ch8-Participating)
choice(""Maybe she's a prisoner here too, and the organizers don't know about her."", Ch8-Prisoner, v_current_scene = Ch8-Prisoner)


ID: Ch8-Disguise
TEXT:

 "Maybe she's an animal in disguise."

"Illusion magic from a forest beast?" Daren frowns. "Unless you think she's wearing a very convincing child costume."

"It doesn't matter who she is," Kate cuts in. "She knows these ruins, and if she served the beasts, she would have sounded an alarm already. There's only one path forward. We follow her and judge her intentions as we go."

We catch up to Flower just as her voice shifts. The tone drops—sharp, frigid, and commanding. She keeps walking, her back to us.

"What are you thinking, Flower?" she mutters in that cold voice. "We came down here to train, not to play tour guide to strangers we found wandering the halls!"

"Relax, Petal!" Flower replies in her own bright, cheerful register. "They're harmless. We can get right back to flips once we drop them off at the button room. It won't take long!"

"Who are you talking to?" Kate asks.

Flower jolts, whirling around with wide eyes.

"D-did we say that out loud?" She catches herself, waving her hands. "I mean me! I! There is only one of me!"

"Are you suggesting there are two people in there?" Daren asks, eyeing her with growing suspicion.

"What? No! That's absurd. You're absurd!"

She bursts into high, breathless, completely unnatural laughter.

"Did she just call me absurd?" Daren mutters.

A muffled cackle echoes from the golden amulet hanging at her throat. Flower unclasps the locket, glaring down at it.

"Quiet, Arraka!" she hisses.

The sound carries through the open casing—three distinct female voices laughing simultaneously in discordant harmony. Realizing she has an audience, the presence in the amulet speaks directly to us.

"Look at her, fools!" the chorus rasps. "The girl houses a banshee! Check her aura! Feel the—"

Flower snaps the amulet shut, cutting the voice off, but the damage is done.

I reach out with my magical sense. Her aura is massive—willfully throttled down to mimic an ordinary human child. But it isn't simple possession. Two distinct resonances inhabit that small frame: one earthen and warm, the other cold, sharp, and outworldly. Two independent souls coexisting within a single body. It should be impossible.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Banshee, v_current_scene = Ch8-Banshee)


ID: Ch8-Participating
TEXT:

 "Maybe she's also participating in the tournament."

"A ten-year-old child entered in a lethal blood tournament?" Daren mutters. "Not everyone shares your reckless streak, Barry."

"It doesn't matter who she is," Kate cuts in. "She knows these ruins, and if she served the beasts, she would have sounded an alarm already. There's only one path forward. We follow her and judge her intentions as we go."

We catch up to Flower just as her voice shifts. The tone drops—sharp, frigid, and commanding. She keeps walking, her back to us.

