choice("Continue", Ch8-Banshee, v_current_scene = Ch8-Banshee)


ID: Ch8-Banshee
TEXT:

 "So that's what she's hiding," Daren says, his hand dropping to his pommel.

He takes a step toward Flower, his expression softening into practiced bedside assurance.

"You're in luck, child," he says. "You don't have to live under this curse any longer. I happen to be a knight of the Eastern continent and a seasoned white mage. I'll sever this banshee parasite from your spirit in moments."

"What?" Flower shrinks back, eyes wide. "No! You can't!"

"I can," Daren insists, taking another stride forward. "The collar won't stop me. My blade carries purification enchantments strong enough to cleanse an entity without casting a fresh spell. We will destroy the banshee, and you can live a normal life."

"No!" Flower shouts, planting her bare feet. "She's my friend! I won't let you touch her!"

"Friend?" Daren's brow furrows with grave concern. "The corruption is deeper than I thought. Hold still, girl. You aren't in your right mind—"

Under Daren's heavy armored boot, a flagstone gives way with a hollow clunk.

Gears grind violently in the ceiling above.

"Look up!" Flower yells.

A massive granite slab shears loose from the ceiling, plunging straight toward us. Flower snaps her palm toward the falling boulder. A roaring sphere of flame erupts from her hand, detonating against the rock in a blinding flash that pulverizes it into gravel and smoke.

Grit showers over our heads. Before the dust settles, a deep groan reverberates through the foundations, and the side walls begin grinding inward, closing the hallway into a crushing vise.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Trap, v_current_scene = Ch8-Trap)


ID: Ch8-Trap
TEXT:

 "Oh, no," Flower gasps, scanning the contracting walls. "I remember this one! It won't stop until it presses us into paste!"

Her gaze darts around the corridor, locking onto the breach in the ceiling she dropped through earlier.

"New plan!" she calls out. "I can collapse both ends of the corridor with fireballs, seal the hallway, and flood the chamber with water so we all float up through the ceiling hole! Can you all swim?"

"I am wearing eighty pounds of steel plate," Daren roars over the grinding stone. "What do you think?!"

"Right! Newer plan! The override levers are in the chamber above! Petal, give me a lift!"

Flower drops her palms toward the floor. High-pressure torrents of water shoot from her hands, blasting against the stone with enough force to launch her straight upward, shooting through the ceiling breach.

"What in the hell?" Daren gawks at the hole. "She threw fire a second ago! Has a child mastered two elemental schools?"

"Water belongs to the banshee," I tell him.

"You what?" Daren turns to stare at me.

"Can you hear me down there?" Flower's voice floats down from the opening above. "I found the override console! The issue is... there are twelve different levers. And none of the labels make sense. But I'm sure I'll figure it out in time. Probably!"

The walls are already three feet closer, mortar scraping against the floor with a deafening screech.

"That tears it," Hadrik grunts, rolling his shoulders. "I'm punching an exit through the right wall."

"Don't touch it!" Kate snaps. "Are you out of your mind? If that masonry is load-bearing, you'll bring the entire upper level down on our heads!"

"Rather risk a cave-in than stand here like grain in a millstone!" Hadrik retorts. "You honestly expect that child to solve an ancient puzzle before we're flat as parchment?"

"Down there!" Flower calls through the gap. "Forgot one minor detail! Whatever you do, do NOT smash the walls! Got it? Great! Now let's see... Aha! No, that was the light switch. Back to work!"

choice("Tell Hadrik to ignore Kate and Flower and to smash through the wall", Ch8-Smash, v_current_scene = Ch8-Smash, v_ch8_smash = 1)
choice("Try to convince Hadrik to wait a little longer for Flower", Ch8-Wait, v_current_scene = Ch8-Wait, v_ch8_smash = 0)


ID: Ch8-Smash
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_reflexes < 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_reflexes >= 2)
#if(v_reflexes < 2) {
 

"Hadrik, there's no time! Just tear down that wall, and we'll worry about the consequences later."

"Hah!" Hadrik grins. "That's what I wanted to hear! Stand clear!"

The dwarf unleashes a devastating punch into the advancing wall. The masonry implodes, but behind the shattered stone, a spring-loaded trap triggers. A volley of iron spears erupts from the breach at point-blank range.

I see the iron tips emerge—a wall of death racing toward me—and my body simply cannot move fast enough. Time stretches into a single frozen heartbeat where I know exactly what is about to happen and can do nothing to stop it.

An iron spear punches through my chest, pinning me upright against the stone behind. A second takes my throat. The pain is white and total and then nothing—just the distant sound of Daren shouting my name as everything goes dark.

}
#if(v_reflexes >= 2) {
 

"Hadrik, there's no time! Just tear down that wall, and we'll worry about the consequences later."

"Hah!" Hadrik grins. "That's what I wanted to hear! Stand clear!"

The dwarf unleashes a devastating punch into the advancing wall. The masonry implodes, but behind the shattered stone, a spring-loaded trap triggers. A volley of iron spears erupts from the breach at point-blank range.

My reflexes take over before thought can catch up. I throw myself flat against the floor as an iron spear whistles through the air where my head was half a heartbeat ago, burying itself deep in the opposite stone. The others react just as swiftly—Hadrik and Kate twist clear of the volley, while Daren catches two spears clean on his heavy steel shield, deflecting them into the dust.

Above us, the grinding mechanisms shudder and groan to a halt.

A pair of bare feet drops through the ceiling hole, landing lightly on the flagstones. Flower stands there, beaming with pride.

"I stopped it!" she announces, then freezes, taking in the splintered spears and pulverized wall. "What happened? Did someone smash the wall? I explicitly said NOT to smash the wall!"

"We heard you," Kate says dryly. "Certain members of our party simply process verbal instructions with a distinct delay."

"Oh!" Flower looks genuinely contrite. "I should have yelled louder. Is anyone injured? Petal knows basic healing if you took a hit."

"We're intact," Hadrik mutters, rubbing his knuckles. "Got a little impatient, is all."

"Right," Flower says, her smile turning nervous. "Now for the other news. While I was toggling levers upstairs... I may have accidentally armed every single trap in this entire corridor."

"You did what?" Kate's voice turns dangerously cold.

"I can guide us through!" Flower insists quickly. "I know where most of the triggers are! I just need to run a quick test to refresh my memory."

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_reflexes < 2)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_reflexes < 2)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_reflexes < 2)
choice("Continue", Ch8-Dare, v_current_scene = Ch8-Dare) if (v_reflexes >= 2)


ID: Ch8-Wait
TEXT:

 "Hadrik, it's too risky. Can't you give Flower just a little more time?"

Hadrik grunts, clearly irritated by the lack of enthusiasm for brute force.

"Fine," he mutters, lowering his fists. "I'll wait. But the second those stones touch my shoulders, I'm bringing the roof down."

The walls close to within arm's length before the screech of grinding gears slows, shuddering into silence.

Flower drops through the hole in the ceiling, landing neatly on the flagstones with a triumphant grin.

"I stopped it!" she beams. "Though... there is a small complication. While I was toggling levers upstairs, I may have accidentally armed every single trap in this entire corridor."

"You did what?" Kate's voice turns dangerously cold.

"I can guide us through!" Flower insists quickly. "I know where most of the triggers are! I just need to run a quick test to refresh my memory."

choice("Continue", Ch8-Dare, v_current_scene = Ch8-Dare)


ID: Ch8-Dare
TEXT:

 Flower bolts down the hallway. She launches herself in a breathtaking leap, landing lightly on a cracked flagstone fifteen feet ahead, spins on one heel, and faces us with a grin.

"See? Completely under con—"

A recessed slot in the masonry snaps open, and a crescent pendulum blade swings out, sweeping toward her chest.

Flower drops into a fluid roll. Her heel clips a pressure plate, and the corridor explodes into motion. Arrows hiss from wall slits in dense crossfire while jagged, spinning iron discs rise from floor grooves, carving circles in the stone.

It looks chaotic at a glance, but watching her rhythm reveals the training. Every dodge flows seamlessly into the next—a vault over a floor blade feeding directly into a wall-kick that clears a volley of darts. She wastes neither motion nor momentum.

Hadrik shakes his head at the spectacle, drops flat on his stomach, and presses his ear against the floor stones.

"I know it looks messy!" Flower shouts over the whistling darts as she rebounds off the left wall with one hand. "If I keep moving, I'll either remember the safe tiles or exhaust all the mechanisms! Either way, we win!"

"Aye, and the golden fox will be on our necks before you finish your dance," Hadrik says, pushing himself up. "This hall is a deathtrap. But there's open space below us. Hollow stone, running water, and movement. I'm making us a shortcut."

"Don't you dare!" Kate warns, stepping back.

"Can't hear a word over the blades!" Hadrik roars, grinning.

He drives both fists into the flagstones beneath our boots.

The floor buckles, fractures, and disintegrates into a gaping pit. The world drops out beneath us, and we tumble through the darkness in a roar of tumbling masonry.

We hit bottom with a heavy thud. The impact is surprisingly cushioned, the surface yielding under our weight rather than shattering our limbs.

"Hadrik, you reckless idiot!" Kate screams, struggling to her feet in the gloom. "Do you think the rest of us share your giant constitution? If this soft pile hadn't broken the drop, we'd all have shattered legs! If I had my ice magic, I'd freeze you into a block and leave you here!"

Beneath my palms, the ground heaves with a rhythmic, muscular rise and fall.

Above us in the darkness, a low, reverberating hiss echoes through the cavern.

choice("Examine the surface more closely", Ch8-Surface, v_current_scene = Ch8-Surface)
choice("Try to identify the source of the sound", Ch8-Sound, v_current_scene = Ch8-Sound)


ID: Ch8-Surface
TEXT:

 I run my palm across the ground. The texture is cold, slick, and ridged with overlapping dark green scales as thick as armor plates. My stomach drops before I even glance up.

Towering above us in the subterranean gloom are nine massive serpent heads, each thick as a tree trunk, fangs dripping venomous slime as they sway in unison. All nine necks merge into the colossal reptilian torso currently cushioning our landing. I have read the bestiary folios on them—there is no mistaking the silhouette. We are sitting directly on the back of a live hydra.

Kate and Hadrik are still trading insults, oblivious. Daren is only now running a gauntleted hand over the scaled hide beneath his knees, while Rose stares straight up into the swaying canopy of fangs, paralyzed with terror.

"Hadrik. Kate," I say, keeping my voice low and level. "Look up."

Both of them freeze.

"Merciful ancestors," Hadrik breathes, his grin vanishing.

"Off it! Now!" Daren roars, scooping Rose into one armored arm as he launches himself toward the flagstones.

I roll down the slick flank, hitting the floor and scrambling back. We draw our blades and fan out across the cavern floor. The hydra shifts its bulk with a grinding scrape of scales against stone. All nine heads hiss in discord, its thick, muscular tail sweeping side to side as it advances.

One serpent neck coils and strikes downward. The strike is heavy and telegraphed; we scatter to the sides as the snout slams into the stone wall behind us, blasting a crater in the masonry.

Daren closes the distance in two strides, his enchanted broadsword flashing in a clean silver arc that lops the serpent head cleanly from its neck.

"Don't!" I yell. "Why did you do that?"

The hydra violently whips the bleeding stump back into the pack, the remaining eight heads shrieking in piercing fury. Within heartbeats, flesh knits, bone sprouts, and the severed head re-forms completely, baring a fresh set of fangs.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Hydra, v_current_scene = Ch8-Hydra)


ID: Ch8-Sound
TEXT:

 I tilt my head toward the guttural rumble in the dark ceiling.

Towering above us in the subterranean gloom are nine massive serpent heads, each thick as a tree trunk, fangs dripping venomous slime as they sway in unison. All nine necks merge into the colossal reptilian torso currently cushioning our landing. I have read the bestiary folios on them—there is no mistaking the silhouette. We are sitting directly on the back of a live hydra.

Kate and Hadrik are still trading insults, oblivious. Daren is only now running a gauntleted hand over the scaled hide beneath his knees, while Rose stares straight up into the swaying canopy of fangs, paralyzed with terror.

"Hadrik. Kate," I say, keeping my voice low and level. "Look up."

Both of them freeze.

"Merciful ancestors," Hadrik breathes, his grin vanishing.

"Off it! Now!" Daren roars, scooping Rose into one armored arm as he launches himself toward the flagstones.

I roll down the slick flank, hitting the floor and scrambling back. We draw our blades and fan out across the cavern floor. The hydra shifts its bulk with a grinding scrape of scales against stone. All nine heads hiss in discord, its thick, muscular tail sweeping side to side as it advances.

One serpent neck coils and strikes downward. The strike is heavy and telegraphed; we scatter to the sides as the snout slams into the stone wall behind us, blasting a crater in the masonry.

Daren closes the distance in two strides, his enchanted broadsword flashing in a clean silver arc that lops the serpent head cleanly from its neck.

"Don't!" I yell. "Why did you do that?"

The hydra violently whips the bleeding stump back into the pack, the remaining eight heads shrieking in piercing fury. Within heartbeats, flesh knits, bone sprouts, and the severed head re-forms completely, baring a fresh set of fangs.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Hydra, v_current_scene = Ch8-Hydra)


ID: Ch8-Hydra
TEXT:

 "What?" Daren steps back, raising his shield. "You didn't actually believe the old tavern tales about two heads sprouting for every one you sever? I've fought hydras on the Eastern continent. None of them do that. But this beast regenerates far faster than any specimen I've seen. Usually you have time to decapitate every neck in succession, but we can't outpace this rate. The only way to put it down is finding and piercing the core heart, or burning the stumps to seal the tissue."

"Damn it all," Kate grunts, her hand gripping her dagger. "If my ice magic were unlocked, I could shear all nine necks in a single sweep."

"The girl uses fire," Daren says, glancing up at the ceiling breach. He cups a hand to his mouth. "Flower! Flower, down here!"

Nothing answers except the whistle of spinning iron discs and clattering darts from the floor above.

"Save your lungs," Hadrik says. "She won't hear a shout over fifty tripwire traps firing at once."

"Right," Daren mutters, resetting his stance.

The hydra coils back slightly, its nine heads weaving cautiously, tracking Daren's blade. The swift decapitation has made it wary.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Hearing-fail, v_current_scene = Ch8-Hearing-fail) if (v_hearing < 4)
choice("Continue", Ch8-Hearing-success, v_current_scene = Ch8-Hearing-success) if (v_hearing == 4)


ID: Ch8-Hearing-fail
TEXT:

 

"If the beast won't move," Hadrik grunts, "I will."

He charges. Four serpent necks strike at him simultaneously, but Hadrik ducks low, slides under the snapping fangs, and wedges his broad shoulders beneath the hydra's underbelly. With a bellow that rattles the cavern walls, he heaves upward, veins bulging along his neck and temples.

He lifts the multi-ton behemoth clean off the flagstones and hurls it across the chamber.

The hydra slams into the far wall with a bone-jarring crash, its necks flailing as it scrambles to right itself.

"I won't waste the opening!" Daren shouts. "Barry, stay with Rose! Hadrik and I will keep it pinned!"

He sprints forward, sword carving deep rents into the beast's flank.

I look back. Rose sits huddled against the stone, arms wrapped tight around her shins, trembling uncontrollably.

choice("Try to help her shake off the fear", Ch8-Shake, v_current_scene = Ch8-Shake)
choice("Leave her alone", Ch8-Alone, v_current_scene = Ch8-Alone)
choice(""Are you seriously going to do this every time we fight a big monster?"", Ch8-Seriously, v_current_scene = Ch8-Seriously)


ID: Ch8-Hearing-success
TEXT:

 

A rhythmic thudding pulses through the chamber.

I close my eyes for a fraction of a second, filtering out Hadrik's heavy breathing, Daren's clinking plate, and the traps clattering above. The pulse is deep, wet, and heavy—the beast's cardiovascular core. I track the acoustic resonance through the stone. It isn't in the chest cavity, nor near the juncture of the necks. The thrum originates at the very tip of its thick tail, buried beneath heavy scales.

"If the beast won't move," Hadrik grunts, "I will."

He charges. Four serpent necks strike at him simultaneously, but Hadrik ducks low, slides under the snapping fangs, and wedges his broad shoulders beneath the hydra's underbelly. With a bellow that rattles the cavern walls, he heaves upward, veins bulging along his neck and temples.

He lifts the multi-ton behemoth clean off the flagstones and hurls it across the chamber.

The hydra slams into the far wall with a bone-jarring crash, its necks flailing as it scrambles to right itself.

choice("Use this opportunity to rush towards the hydra and cut off its heart", Ch8-Rush, v_current_scene = Ch8-Rush)
choice("Tell Daren about the hydra's weak spot", Ch8-Weakspot, v_current_scene = Ch8-Weakspot)


ID: Ch8-Shake
TEXT:

 "Rose!"

She gives no indication of hearing me, her gaze locked on the flagstones as the shivers wrack her frame.

"Rose. Look at me."

"Leave her," Kate says quietly from beside me. "She'll steady once the danger clears. It was the same against Tyrath. She's holding on as best she can."

"Right," I say, turning back toward the melee.

Hadrik and Daren have their hands full. The hydra lashes out with multiple necks at once, forcing Hadrik to swat heads aside with his forearms while Daren probes the thick torso with swift thrusts, searching for a vital organ in vain. Every gouge in the hide seals almost as quickly as the blade withdraws.

They fall back a few paces to reset their footing.

A column of roaring crimson flame plunges from the ceiling, engulfing the hydra from snout to tail. All nine heads shriek in unified torment as the fire sears through scale, muscle, and bone in seconds. The howls choke out, and the beast collapses into a charred, smoking heap.

As the inferno subsides, Flower floats down through the ceiling breach, cushions of fire flaring from the soles of her bare feet to slow her descent.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Awakened, v_current_scene = Ch8-Awakened)


ID: Ch8-Alone
TEXT:

 Empty reassurances won't help her right now. She will steady once the threat is dead. I keep myself positioned between Rose and the beast, watching the battle unfold.

Hadrik and Daren have their hands full. The hydra lashes out with multiple necks at once, forcing Hadrik to swat heads aside with his forearms while Daren probes the thick torso with swift thrusts, searching for a vital organ in vain. Every gouge in the hide seals almost as quickly as the blade withdraws.

They fall back a few paces to reset their footing.

A column of roaring crimson flame plunges from the ceiling, engulfing the hydra from snout to tail. All nine heads shriek in unified torment as the fire sears through scale, muscle, and bone in seconds. The howls choke out, and the beast collapses into a charred, smoking heap.

As the inferno subsides, Flower floats down through the ceiling breach, cushions of fire flaring from the soles of her bare feet to slow her descent.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Awakened, v_current_scene = Ch8-Awakened)


ID: Ch8-Seriously
TEXT:

 "Are you seriously going to do this every time we fight a big monster?"

A sharp, driving punch catches me square in the solar plexus. The air leaves my lungs in a breathless wheeze as I drop to one knee.

"Tactful as ever," Kate says coldly, pulling her fist back.

I drag air back into my chest and push myself up. "You know, Kate... with your ice spells locked away, I could actually return the favor."

"Try it," Kate says, dropping instantly into a grounded martial stance, knuckles squared. "Device enhancements and all. I trained hand-to-hand long before I picked up magic."

Even stripped of her casting, her gaze is pure steel.

"A joke," I wheeze, raising an open palm. "Only a joke."

Kate drops her stance, leaning against the damp wall with arms folded over her chest.

In the center of the chamber, Hadrik and Daren have their hands full. The hydra lashes out with multiple necks at once, forcing Hadrik to swat heads aside with his forearms while Daren probes the thick torso with swift thrusts, searching for a vital organ in vain. Every gouge in the hide seals almost as quickly as the blade withdraws.

They fall back a few paces to reset their footing.

A column of roaring crimson flame plunges from the ceiling, engulfing the hydra from snout to tail. All nine heads shriek in unified torment as the fire sears through scale, muscle, and bone in seconds. The howls choke out, and the beast collapses into a charred, smoking heap.

As the inferno subsides, Flower floats down through the ceiling breach, cushions of fire flaring from the soles of her bare feet to slow her descent.

choice("Continue", Ch8-Awakened, v_current_scene = Ch8-Awakened)


ID: Ch8-Rush
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch8_hydra,1) if (v_agility >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility >= 3)
achievement("Hydra slayer",v_ac_ch8_hydra)
#if(v_agility < 3) {
 

I draw my dagger and sprint toward the staggering monster while its balance is broken.

Even dazed, the beast reacts. Two serpent heads whip toward me. I dive sideways to clear the first strike, then scramble toward the tail to drive my blade into the heart. The hydra registers the threat, whipping its tail high out of reach.

The creature recovers its footing, fanning all nine heads in an enclosing arc. I evade two lunges, but the third catches me off balance. Massive fangs punch through my chest. My vision blurs to black before I even hit the stone.

}
#if(v_agility >= 3) {
 

I draw my dagger and sprint toward the staggering monster while its balance is broken.

Two serpent heads lash out, but my boosted speed carries me under the snap of their jaws before they can close. I surge toward the tail, blade raised, but the hydra senses the angle and hoists its tail high toward the ceiling.

It knows its own weak point.

The creature rebalances, all nine heads weaving to corner me. At this speed, slipping between their lunges is manageable, but the tail remains ten feet in the air.

"Boy, what in the blazes are you attempting?" Hadrik roars.

"Hadrik! The heart is in the tip of its tail! Pull it down and I'll end it!"

"Say no more!" Hadrik grins.

The dwarf vaults behind the hydra, latches onto the thick scales of the tail with both hands, and hauls down with crushing force.

"Whenever you're ready, lad!" Hadrik strains against the thrashing muscle.

I accelerate in a blur across the flagstones, drive my dagger up to the hilt into the tail's core, and twist the steel.

A hideous, choking shriek tears from all nine throats simultaneously. The heads thrash wildly, then go limp one by one as the massive carcass hits the stone with a deafening thud.

"Barry, you glory-hunting rogue!" Daren shouts, jogging over. "You could have passed the word on the weak point, but you had to have the trophy for yourself. Slain your first hydra—going to let it inflate your ego?"

"Standard procedure," I say, wiping the dagger on my boot. "I planned on legendary monster hunts after claiming the Magium anyway."

Daren chuckles, shaking his head. "You arrogant little—"

He cuts off as Flower floats down through the ceiling opening, jets of flame hissing from her bare feet to cushion her landing.

"A hydra down here?" she gasps, looking around at the carcass. "I would have hurried, but the tripwires above wouldn't stop firing!"

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Continue", Ch8-Awakened-win, v_current_scene = Ch8-Awakened-win) if (v_agility >= 3)


ID: Ch8-Weakspot
TEXT:

 "Daren!" I call out. "The heart isn't in the chest! It's in the tip of the tail!"

"Are you certain?" Daren calls back over his shoulder.

"My Hearing stat is maxed out. I can hear the pulse thumping from here."

"Good enough for me," Daren says, pivoting on his heel.

He charges the recovering beast. Two heads whip down to intercept him; Daren catches one on his shield, shears the other with a backhand slash, and surges toward the tail. But the hydra jerks its tail upward, hoisting the organ high above Daren's reach.

"Hoisting your weak point, are you?" Daren mutters. "Then I'll take the whole limb."

He springs upward, channeling his momentum into an overhead chop at the root of the tail. The enchanted broadsword cuts clean through scale and bone, severing the tail completely.

A deafening shriek erupts from every throat. The thrashing necks stiffen, go slack, and the massive bulk crashes onto the stone floor, dead.

"Bizarre anatomy," Daren pants, lowering his blade. "How have hydras survived extinction with a flaw like that?"

"Because warriors like you hack at the torso and ignore the tail," Kate replies smoothly. "You fought them on the Eastern continent and never checked. I'd say their diversionary tactics work remarkably well."

Daren scowls, sheathing his sword without a rebuttal.

Above us, Flower floats down through the ceiling opening, cushions of flame flaring from her feet as she lands on the flagstones.

"A hydra down here?" she gasps, looking around at the dead beast. "I would have hurried, but the tripwires above wouldn't stop firing!"

choice("Continue", Ch8-Awakened-win, v_current_scene = Ch8-Awakened-win)


ID: Ch8-Awakened
TEXT:

#if(v_ch8_smash == 0) {
 "A hydra down here?" Flower says as she lands on the flagstones. "I would have hurried, but the tripwires above wouldn't stop firing! Is anyone hurt? Petal knows basic healing if you took a hit."

The casual ease with which she incinerated the beast speaks to power far beyond her appearance. At full strength we might hold our own, but stripped of magic, antagonizing her would be madness.

"I could use a touch on this leg," Hadrik says, pointing to a jagged gash across his shin. "Stings like hell."

"We're on it!" Flower trots over and places her small hands over the wound. "Petal?"

Her eyes glaze for a heartbeat, then flare with bright, piercing blue light. Her face settles into a cold, impassive mask as cool white healing energy streams from her palms into the torn flesh.

"So..." Hadrik says with a grin. "You're the banshee sharing the quarters. Petal, is it?"

The girl meets his gaze with unblinking blue eyes, silent and focused, continuing the flow of magic until the skin knits smooth.

"Not much for tavern banter, eh?" Hadrik chuckles.

As the healing light fades, her eyes soften back to emerald green, and Flower's warm expression returns.

"She isn't usually so quiet," Flower says apologetically. "Just shy with new people."

"That's quite enough of this charade," Daren says, stepping forward, his hand resting on his pommel. "I regret breaking up a companionable arrangement, but the banshee must be purged."

"You won't be able to do that," I say.

"Is that so?" Daren turns to me, brow raised. "Enlighten us, expert."

"Because the banshee is fully awakened. She's inhabited that body for decades."

"Nonsense. An awakened banshee warps into a hideous monstrosity. Nothing human remains of the host."

"I've seen an awakening firsthand, Daren. Petal is not dormant. Her presence is fully manifest. Try your purification rite if you doubt me."

Daren grunts. "I intend to."

}
#if(v_ch8_smash == 1) {
