}
choice("Continue", Ch8-Golden-rule, v_current_scene = Ch8-Golden-rule)


ID: Ch8-Golden-rule
TEXT:

 "Hold!" the leopard speaks in the common tongue, his voice deep and measured.

Flower blinks, the crimson glare in her eyes gradually subsiding to soft emerald green.

"What is the meaning of this, Leo?" Eleya's amber eyes snap toward him. "You are permitted the common speech only under dire emergency."

"I apologize for the breach, Great Fox," Leo says, bowing his head slightly. "Yet this matter constitutes an emergency of the highest order."

"State your reason."

"I invoke the Sixth Golden Rule and claim personal custody of these prisoners."

"To what purpose?"

"They are far more valuable to us living than dead. We can spare no more beast warriors against the ogre stronghold. At this rate, the sacred chalice will remain lost forever. Yet these outsiders proved their martial worth by slaying the subterranean hydra. We can dispatch them to recover the chalice in exchange for their freedom."

Eleya studies him, the golden aura settling into a calm, steady hum.

"So this is why you requested to accompany me to the console room upon their escape. You surprise me, Leo. Of all my subjects, your hatred for humankind runs deepest. I never foresaw you advocating for human instruments in our service."

She considers the proposal in silence.

"Very well. In accordance with the Sixth Golden Rule, full custody of the five prisoners is granted to you."

Eleya turns her gaze upon our cage.

"You have been granted an extraordinary reprieve, humans. See that you do not waste it."

choice("Ask her about the ogre stronghold", Ch8-Stronghold, v_current_scene = Ch8-Stronghold)
choice("Ask her about the sacred chalice", Ch8-Chalice, v_current_scene = Ch8-Chalice)


ID: Ch8-Stronghold
TEXT:

 "Could you tell us more about this ogre stronghold we are about to be sent to?"

"The fortress lies several dozen leagues from here," Eleya says. "The ogres have established it as their regional redoubt over recent seasons. It is heavily fortified, garrisoned by seasoned warriors, and protected by several powerful shamans."

"Will you deactivate our collars during the mission?" Kate asks. "I am familiar with these mechanisms. They can be temporarily toggled without total removal."

"These collars are primitive prototypes," Eleya replies. "Their suppression field persists until physically unlatched. I will not remove them until the sacred chalice is in my possession. You have a window of five days. If you fail to return before the fifth sunset, I will assume desertion and trigger the collars' lethal discharge."

"Five days?" Hadrik grunts. "What if we lose the trail?"

"You will not," Eleya says. "I am providing a guide who knows the terrain."

choice("Continue", Ch8-Ending, v_current_scene = Ch8-Ending)


ID: Ch8-Chalice
TEXT:

 "Could you tell us more about this sacred chalice that we are meant to retrieve?"

"The chalice is an ancient relic that infuses water with restorative essence," Eleya says. "It cures afflictions unique to beastkind that conventional spells cannot touch. Since the ogres raided our sanctum and stole the vessel, those sicknesses have claimed scores of my subjects."

"Will you deactivate our collars during the mission?" Kate asks. "I am familiar with these mechanisms. They can be temporarily toggled without total removal."

"These collars are primitive prototypes," Eleya replies. "Their suppression field persists until physically unlatched. I will not remove them until the sacred chalice is in my possession. You have a window of five days. If you fail to return before the fifth sunset, I will assume desertion and trigger the collars' lethal discharge."

"Five days?" Hadrik grunts. "What if we lose the trail?"

"You will not," Eleya says. "I am providing a guide who knows the terrain."

choice("Continue", Ch8-Ending, v_current_scene = Ch8-Ending)


ID: Ch8-Ending
TEXT:

 Eleya turns her amber gaze upon Flower.

"Flower. Since you were so eager to shield these humans with your life, the duty of guiding them falls to you."

"Uh..." Flower fidgets, tugging at the hem of her shirt. "I don't think they're thrilled with my guiding skills after the ruin tour... Couldn't Leo go instead, or—"

"You are assigned the task. Consider it penance for raising magic against me. If you refuse the assignment, I will execute them immediately and spare you the march."

"No!" Flower waves her hands frantically. "I'll go! I'll guide them to the ogre fort!"

"So be it," Eleya says, turning toward the archway. "Leo will provide the tactical briefing. I have other duties requiring my presence."

As the golden fox departs, Flower turns to face us, her hands clasped behind her back.

"So..." she offers a small, sheepish grin. "Looks like we're traveling together a while longer."

Her laugh is high, nervous, and thoroughly unconvincing.

Even without checking the premonition stat, one conclusion is inescapable: this journey is going to be chaotic.

choice("Next chapter", Ch9-Intro, v_next_chapter_crash = 1, v_current_scene = Ch9-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, special:checkpoint_save)
